WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:18.976
"We knew Maggie yelled at Joey.

2
00:00:18.996 --> 00:00:21.898
"You slashed those tires, didn't you?"

3
00:00:21.918 --> 00:00:23.339
"It wasn't me!"

4
00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:24.880
Joey pointed at Tina.

5
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.502
"She probably did it, and now she's trying to blame it on me!"

6
00:00:29.423 --> 00:00:30.344
Tina gasped.

7
00:00:31.768 --> 00:00:33.369
"I did not do it!"

8
00:00:34.429 --> 00:00:36.430
All the commotion was attracting attention.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.111
"What's going on?"

10
00:00:38.431 --> 00:00:39.992
Ashley asked, hurrying over.

11
00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:43.313
"This kid slashed the tires!"

12
00:00:43.813 --> 00:00:45.514
Maggie cried, pointing at Joey.

13
00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:49.255
"I already told you dummies that I didn't do it!"

14
00:00:49.596 --> 00:00:50.356
Joey yelled.

15
00:00:51.376 --> 00:00:52.537
Maggie glared at him.

16
00:00:52.557 --> 00:00:54.838
"Why should we believe you?

17
00:00:55.718 --> 00:00:57.219
We heard you teasing Nathan.

18
00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.480
So we already know you're a bully!"

19
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.961
More people had arrived by then.

20
00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:06.202
"Wait," the Belltown cheerleader named Melanie spoke up.

21
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:08.103
"He's telling the truth.

22
00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:09.864
He didn't do it."

23
00:01:09.884 --> 00:01:11.645
"How do you know?"

24
00:01:12.025 --> 00:01:12.705
Jill asked.

25
00:01:12.725 --> 00:01:17.847
"Because I saw him hanging out right here by the restrooms," Melanie said.

26
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:21.969
"I was down here for most of the break because I had a stomachache.

27
00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.169
He was here the whole time."

28
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:26.070
"Are you sure?"

29
00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.131
Ashley asked.

30
00:01:27.991 --> 00:01:30.092
"Maybe he sneaked away while you weren't looking."

31
00:01:31.388 --> 00:01:32.228
Melanie laughed.

32
00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:34.830
"Are you kidding?

33
00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.371
Those Valley High colors are so bright you can't miss them.

34
00:01:39.252 --> 00:01:41.773
I would have noticed if he left even for a second."

35
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:44.114
"Oh." Ashley shrugged.

36
00:01:44.134 --> 00:01:49.276
"Okay, I guess he couldn't have slashed the tires after all."

37
00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:50.997
Just then Ms.

38
00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:52.057
Hernandez arrived.

39
00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.298
"What's all the yelling over here?"

40
00:01:54.318 --> 00:01:56.559
"Nothing," Jill said.

41
00:01:56.579 --> 00:01:58.220
"We were just talking."

42
00:01:59.132 --> 00:02:01.833
Joey and Tina stomped off in opposite directions.

43
00:02:03.613 --> 00:02:05.494
Soon most of the other kids wandered away.

44
00:02:12.676 --> 00:02:14.736
Henry led his friends to a private spot.

45
00:02:14.756 --> 00:02:17.757
"I guess Joey didn't do it," he said.

46
00:02:17.777 --> 00:02:19.578
"He has an alibi."

47
00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:21.638
"What's an alibi?"

48
00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:22.779
Maggie asked.

49
00:02:22.799 --> 00:02:28.736
"It's when someone can prove that he or she wasn't at the scene of the crime," Henry said.

50
00:02:28.756 --> 00:02:33.318
"Joey's alibi is that Melanie saw him by the restrooms.

51
00:02:34.278 --> 00:02:37.899
That means he couldn't have been down at the bikes slashing tires."

52
00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:40.420
"Okay," Maggie said.

53
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.680
"I guess he's not the culprit.

54
00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.921
But what about Tina?

55
00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:47.622
Melanie didn't say anything about seeing her."

56
00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:52.463
"Yeah. And a few people said she disappeared for a while," Cole added.

57
00:02:52.483 --> 00:02:56.064
"She's still a suspect, I guess," Henry said.

58
00:02:57.092 --> 00:02:59.975
"But we shouldn't focus only on the Valley High kids.

59
00:03:00.635 --> 00:03:01.916
There are other suspects."

60
00:03:02.857 --> 00:03:08.242
Just then he spotted the stranger in the sunglasses walking along, muttering into a cell phone.

61
00:03:08.262 --> 00:03:11.985
"Like him, for instance," he whispered.

62
00:03:12.005 --> 00:03:14.707
"Did either of you question him earlier?"

63
00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:18.030
"Nope," Maggie said while Cole shook his head.

64
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.152
"Let's talk to him now," Henry said.

65
00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:25.116
They hurried after the man, who was heading toward the bike rack.

66
00:03:27.548 --> 00:03:28.889
On the way they passed Ms.

67
00:03:28.929 --> 00:03:30.449
Hernandez talking to William.

68
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.030
He looked upset.

69
00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.731
"Why can't I leave now?"

70
00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:35.771
he whined.

71
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:38.773
"My bike is ruined, and I want to go home."

72
00:03:39.753 --> 00:03:40.974
Ms. Hernandez sighed.

73
00:03:40.994 --> 00:03:42.854
"Please be patient.

74
00:03:43.555 --> 00:03:45.315
The new tires will be here soon."

75
00:03:45.335 --> 00:03:49.777
"They probably won't even fit my bike," William argued.

76
00:03:49.797 --> 00:03:52.338
"Anyway this ride is no fun."

77
00:03:52.358 --> 00:03:55.199
"Why does he want to quit the bike ride?"

78
00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.360
Maggie whispered.

79
00:03:57.216 --> 00:04:00.017
"Maybe he feels guilty because he committed the crime."

80
00:04:00.037 --> 00:04:03.939
"But his tire got slashed too," Cole whispered.

81
00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:06.240
"Why would he ruin his own tire?"

82
00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.622
"Maybe he did it so nobody would suspect him," Henry said.

83
00:04:10.642 --> 00:04:14.204
"We can question him after we talk to the mystery man."

84
00:04:15.084 --> 00:04:15.964
They kept going.

85
00:04:16.665 --> 00:04:20.626
The man in the sunglasses stopped near his own bike and finished up his call.

86
00:04:20.646 --> 00:04:23.968
"Hi," Henry said, walking up to the man.

87
00:04:25.008 --> 00:04:27.489
"It looks like your tires didn't get slashed, huh?

88
00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:28.890
That's lucky."

89
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.550
The man shrugged.

90
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.111
"I suppose so.

91
00:04:32.731 --> 00:04:34.692
But only nine tires were damaged."

92
00:04:37.093 --> 00:04:38.794
Henry traded a look with his friends.

93
00:04:39.694 --> 00:04:42.915
How did this man know exactly how many tires had been slashed?

94
00:04:43.956 --> 00:04:45.096
It seemed suspicious.

95
00:04:45.116 --> 00:04:47.897
"How did you hear about this bike ride?"

96
00:04:48.177 --> 00:04:48.958
Cole asked.

97
00:04:49.918 --> 00:04:52.099
"Most of the riders are from the Belltown schools.

98
00:04:52.779 --> 00:04:54.700
I didn't know other people even knew about it."

99
00:04:55.468 --> 00:04:56.408
The man looked away.

100
00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:59.810
"News gets around, I guess," he muttered.

101
00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.231
Henry could tell he didn't want to answer their questions.

102
00:05:03.972 --> 00:05:05.452
That seemed suspicious too.

103
00:05:06.332 --> 00:05:09.894
Luckily Henry's father worked as a reporter at the local newspaper.

104
00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.095
He'd taught Henry a few interviewer's tricks.

105
00:05:14.176 --> 00:05:17.377
One trick was rewording the same question in a different way.

106
00:05:17.397 --> 00:05:20.838
"Did you see a flyer hanging up around town?"

107
00:05:21.138 --> 00:05:21.639
he asked.

108
00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:24.620
"I bet that's how you heard about the ride.

109
00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.721
Or maybe you have a relative that goes to Belltown High."

110
00:05:29.802 --> 00:05:30.582
"Not exactly."

111
00:05:31.202 --> 00:05:32.223
The man looked annoyed.

112
00:05:32.243 --> 00:05:34.684
"Actually I'm a news reporter.

113
00:05:34.704 --> 00:05:36.765
I'm here to cover the story for the local paper."

114
00:05:36.785 --> 00:05:39.346
"What?" Maggie exclaimed.

115
00:05:39.366 --> 00:05:44.148
"But Henry elbowed her in the ribs before she could say anything more.

116
00:05:45.068 --> 00:05:47.069
A second later the stranger hurried off.

117
00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.310
Cole looked confused.

118
00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.231
"What was that all about?

119
00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.552
Does that man work with your dad, Henry?"

120
00:05:54.572 --> 00:05:55.974
"No," Henry said.

121
00:05:55.994 --> 00:06:00.938
"I know all the reporters at the paper, and that guy isn't one of them.

122
00:06:01.679 --> 00:06:02.600
He's lying!"
